# Line endings and diff behaviour.
#
# Deliberately NOT using Git LFS. It was considered and rejected:
#
#   Ghost_v2.blend is 559 KB, because it has no packed HDR and no embedded render result.
#   The original Ghost.tar.xz is 24 MB and the two mp4s are a few MB each, so the whole
#   repository sits around 30 MB. That is fine for a plain clone.
#
#   LFS would cost more than it saves here. It needs `git lfs install` on every machine
#   that clones, GitHub's free tier caps storage and bandwidth at 1 GB per month each, and
#   a portfolio repository that people actually visit can burn that. Worse, adding LFS
#   tracking to files that are already committed does not migrate them: git simply reports
#   them as modified and the next commit replaces the blob with a pointer while the old
#   blob stays in history, so the repository gets bigger, not smaller.
#
# If this ever grows to hold 4K frame sequences or several large .blend revisions, revisit:
#     git lfs install
#     git lfs migrate import --include="*.blend,*.mp4" --everything
# and note that migrate rewrites history, so coordinate it before pushing.

*.blend  binary
*.mp4    binary
*.mov    binary
*.flac   binary
*.wav    binary
*.tar.xz binary

*.py     text
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.md     text
